    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><h2>Calm the Mob</h2><p><em>Crowds don’t think. They feel. So you give them something else to feel.</em></p><hr><h3>Rules</h3><p>You gain a skill rank in Diplomacy (Presence) or Intimidation (Presence) (your choice). If you already have it, its rank rises by one instead.</p><p>When you spend at least 1 minute addressing a group of non-hostile or uncertain creatures, you may make a Presence (Diplomacy (Presence) or Intimidation (Presence)) check (DC set by the GM). On a success, you reduce immediate hostility: the crowd hesitates, disperses, or agrees to hear terms. On a failure, you still buy time, but a complication occurs (a challenger steps forward, guards arrive, a rumor spreads).</p><p class=\"ft-engine-note\"><em>⚙ +1 to Diplomacy or Intimidation — whichever you rank higher.</em></p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
